        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9053b59a-230e-5ae6-bd1c-332187a93f33",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Carvedilol, L-748,328, L-748,337, SR 59,230A, Coreg\n- Concepts: Beta-3 adrenergic antagonists, beta blockers, beta-3 adrenergic receptors\n- Conditions: Congestive heart failure, left ventricular dysfunction, high blood pressure\n\nFacts:\n- Beta-3 adrenergic antagonists are adrenergic antagonists that block beta-3 adrenergic receptors on cells.\n- L-748,328, L-748,337, and SR 59,230A are selective beta-3 adrenergic antagonists.\n- Carvedilol is a non-selective beta blocker that can act as a beta-3 adrenergic antagonist.\n- Carvedilol is sold under the brand name Coreg.\n- Carvedilol is used to treat mild to severe congestive heart failure.\n- Carvedilol is used to treat left ventricular dysfunction after heart attack in otherwise stable people.\n- Carvedilol is used to treat high blood pressure.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
